show that if the weight sequence φ\nis Toeplitz-totally positive, then the two foregoing total-\npositivity results continue to hold. Our proofs use production \nmatrices and exponential Riordan arrays.\n© 2024 The Authors. Published by Elsevier Inc. This is an \nopen access article under the CC BY license (http://\ncreativecommons .org /licenses /by /4 .0/).\nKeywords:\nTree\nLabeled tree\nRooted tree\nFunctional digraph\nPartial functional digraph\nTree function\nLambert W function\nRamanujan polynomials\nRiordan array\n* Corresponding author.\nE-mail addresses: chenxi@dlut.edu.cn (X. Chen), sokal@nyu.edu (A.D. Sokal).\nhttps://doi.org/10.1016/j.aam.2024.102703\n0196-8858/© 2024 The Authors. Published by Elsevier Inc. This is an open access article under the CC \nBY license (http://creativecommons .org /licenses /by /4 .0/).--------------------------------------------------------------------------------\nPlane Triangulations Without Spanning 2-Trees - arXiv Combinatorics (https://arxiv.symmetricfunctions.com/paper/2203.10239v1)\nciteturn1search1 [wordlim: 200] Published: 4.6 years ago; Crawled: 2 months ago; ## Plane Triangulations Without Spanning 2-Trees\n\nAllan Bickle ... graph planar graph plane triangulation spanning tree tree planar\n\n## Plane Triangulations Without Spanning 2-Trees\n\nAllan Bickle\n\nPublished: 2022-03-19\n\nComments: 9 pages\n\nNote:\n\nDOI: 10.26493/1855-3974.3066.5bf\n\ngraph planar graph plane triangulation spanning tree tree planar\n\n# • BIB • PDF • ARXIV •\n\n### Abstract\n\nA 2-tree is a graph that can be formed by starting with a triangle and iterating the operation of making a new vertex adjacent to two adjacent vertices of the existing graph. Leizhen Cai asked in 1995 whether every maximal planar graph contains a spanning 2-tree. We answer this question in the negative by constructing an infinite class of maximal planar graphs that have no spanning 2-tree.\n\n### BibTeX\n\n[Button: arXiv BibTeX ] [Button: Published BibTeX ]\n\nLoading...\n\n[Button: Copy to Clipboard]\n\nLoading...\n\n[Button: Copy to Clipboard]\n\nMaintained by Per Alexandersson, per@symmetricfunctions.com--------------------------------------------------------------------------------\nTotal positivity of some polynomial matrices that enumerate labeled trees and forests. II. Rooted labeled trees and partial functional digraphs (https://arxiv.org/abs/2302.03999)\nciteturn1academia16 [wordlim: 200] Published: 3.7 years ago; Title: Total positivity of some polynomial matrices that enumerate labeled trees and forests. ... Rooted labeled trees and partial functional digraphs\nAuthors: Xi Chen, Alan D. Sokal\nTitle: Total positivity of some polynomial matrices that enumerate labeled trees and forests. II. Rooted labeled trees and partial functional digraphs\nAuthors: Xi Chen, Alan D. Sokal\nDate: Wed Feb  8 11:19:06 2023\n\nWe study three combinatorial models for the lower-triangular matrix with entries $t_{n,k} = \\binom{n}{k} n^{n-k}$: two involving rooted trees on the vertex set $[n+1]$, and one involving partial functional digraphs on the vertex set $[n]$. We show that this matrix is totally positive and that the sequence of its row-generating polynomials is coefficientwise Hankel-totally positive. We then generalize to polynomials $t_{n,k}(y,z)$ that count improper and proper edges, and further to polynomials $t_{n,k}(y,\\mathbf{\\phi})$ in infinitely many indeterminates that give a weight $y$ to each improper edge and a weight $m! \\, \\phi_m$ for each vertex with $m$ proper children. We show that if the weight sequence $\\mathbf{\\phi}$ is Toeplitz-totally positive, then the two foregoing total-positivity results continue to hold. Our proofs use production matrices and exponential Riordan arrays.--------------------------------------------------------------------------------\nPlane triangulations without large 2-trees - MaRDI portal (https://portal.mardi4nfdi.de/wiki/Plane_triangulations_without_large_2-trees)\nciteturn1search2 [wordlim: 200] Published: last year; Crawled: 3 months ago; Authors Allan Bickle, Gunnar Brinkmann ... triangulation Hamiltonian cycle 2-tree Yutsis partition ...   * Plane Triangulations Without Spanning 2-Trees ... This page was built for publication: Plane triangulations without large 2-trees\n# Plane triangulations without large 2-trees\n\nFrom MaRDI portal\n\nJump to:navigation, search\n\nDOI10.26493/1855-3974.3066.5BFMaRDI QIDQ6897931zbMATH OpenFDO\n\nAuthors Allan Bickle, Gunnar Brinkmann\n\nPublication date 19 November 2025\n\nPublished in Ars Mathematica Contemporanea (Search for Journal in Brave)\n\nCopyright license Image Creative Commons Attribution 4.0 International\n\nFull work available at URL https://doi.org/10.26493/1855-3974.3066.5BF\n\nzbMATH Keywords\n\ntriangulationHamiltonian cycle2-treeYutsis partition\n\nMathematics Subject Classification ID\n\nTrees (05C05) Planar graphs; geometric and topological aspects of graph theory (05C10) Eulerian and Hamiltonian graphs (05C45)\n--------------------------------------------------------------------------------\nMonatshefte für Mathematik (https://discovery.ucl.ac.uk/id/eprint/10144793/1/Sokal2022_Article_TotalPositivityOfSomePolynomia.pdf)\nciteturn1search17 [wordlim: 200] Published: 8 months ago; Sokal1,2 ... positive, then the two foregoing total-positivity results continue to hold. ... Keywords Tree · Labeled tree · Rooted tree · Forest · Rooted forest · Functional\nMonatshefte für Mathematik\nhttps://doi.org/10.1007/s00605-022-01687-0\nTotal positivity of some polynomial matrices\nthat enumerate labeled trees and forests I:\nforests of rooted labeled trees\nAlan D. Sokal1,2\nReceived: 11 January 2022 / Accepted: 1 February 2022\n© The Author(s) 2022\nAbstract\nWe consider the lower-triangular matrix of generating polynomials that enumerate\nk-component forests of rooted trees on the vertex set [n] according to the number of\nimproper edges (generalizations of the Ramanujan polynomials). We show that this\nmatrix is coefﬁcientwise totally positive and that the sequence of its row-generating\npolynomials is coefﬁcientwise Hankel-totally positive. More generally, we deﬁne the\ngeneric rooted-forest polynomials by introducing also a weight m! φm for each vertex\nwith m proper children. We show that if the weight sequence φ is Toeplitz-totally\npositive, then the two foregoing total-positivity results continue to hold. Our proofs\nuse production matrices and exponential Riordan arrays.\nKeywords Tree · Labeled tree · Rooted tree · Forest · Rooted forest · Functional\ndigraph · Proper edge · Improper edge · Abel polynomials · Ramanujan\npolynomials · Rooted-forest polynomials · Schläﬂi–Gessel–Seo polynomials ·\nExponential generating function · Exponential Riordan array · Tree function,\nLambert W function · Production matrix · Toeplitz matrix · Hankel matrix · Totally\npositive matrix · Total positivity · Toeplitz-total positivity · Hankel-total positivity ·\nStieltjes moment sequence\nMathematics Subject Classiﬁcation 05A15 (Primary) · 05A19 · 05A20 · 05C05 ·\n05C30 · 15B05 · 15B36 · 15B48 · 30E05 · 44A60 (Secondary)\nCommunicated by Ilse Fischer.\nB Alan D. Sokal\nsokal@nyu.edu\n1\nDepartment of Mathematics, University College London, Gower Street, London WC1E 6BT, UK\n2\nDepartment of Physics, New York University, 726 Broadway, New York, NY 10003, USA\n123--------------------------------------------------------------------------------\nPlane triangulations without large 2-trees (https://www.researchgate.net/publication/387047334_Plane_triangulations_without_large_2-trees)\nciteturn1search3 [wordlim: 200] Published: last year; Crawled: 2 months ago; Bickle and G. ... tree and two such 4-blocks are adjacent if they share a (formerly) separating triangle. ... (a) There are plane triangulations without spanning 2-trees. ... The plane triangulation P 29 has no spanning 2-tree.\n\nconnected or isomorphic to K 4. These 4-blocks are the vertices of the decomposition\n\ntree and two such 4-blocks are adjacent if they share a (formerly) separating triangle.\n\nAccepted manuscript\n\nA. Bickle and G. Brinkmann: Plane triangulations without large 2-trees 5\n\nu\n\nS\n\nN\n\nu’\n\nFigure 1: The graph P 14 . The path N , u, S must be identiﬁed with the path N , u′, S.\n\nCorollary 2.2.\n\n•If P is a plane triangulation with a spanning 2-tree T, then each 4-block has a\n\nspanning 2-tree, so that each formerly separating triangle contains an edge of T.\n\n•If P is a plane triangulation with a spanning 2-tree T, then each 4-block has a\n\nhamiltonian cycle C, so that for one side – which we call the inside – we have that\n\neach formerly separating triangle lies on the inside or contains an edge of C.\n\nProof. The ﬁrst part is a direct consequence of applying Lemma 2.1 to all formerly sepa-\n\nrating triangles of a 4-block subsequently.\n\nThe second part is a consequence of the ﬁrst one as in a 4-block all triangles are faces\n\nand all spanning 2-trees correspond to hamiltonian cycles. The edges of triangles of the\n\n2-tree are the edges of the hamiltonian cycle as well as the edges on one side of it. So the\n\nﬁrst part implies that there is a hamiltonian cycle, so that all separating triangles contain an\n\nedge on the cycle or on one ﬁxed side of it.\n\nNow we can answer the question from [7]:\n\nCorollary 2.3.\n\n(a) There are plane triangulations without spanning 2-trees.\n\n(b) For each orientable or non-orientable surface there are triangulations without span-\n\nning 2-trees.\n\nProof. Statement (a) was ﬁrst proven in [1] by giving an example on 38 vertices, but is also\n\na consequence of Corollary 2.2 and Theorem 3.1 in [4] where a plane triangulation is given\n\nwhere for each hamiltonian cycle C triangles without edges of C exist on both sides of C.\n\nIn Lemma 2.4 we will present a smaller counterexample and prove that it has no spanning\n\n----------------------------------------------------------